## 📝 Step-by-Step Build Guide

### 🧬 A Full System Clone

The ISO is a copy of the system you run it on. Your own **users, passwords, settings and `/home`** are copied exactly as they are. **No live account is created** and nothing is added to or changed inside the clone.

Only these are left out: `dev`, `proc`, `sys`, `run`, `tmp`, `mnt`, `media`, the work folder, and files that stop a live boot (`fstab`, `crypttab`, `mtab`, swap and the persistent udev rules).

### 1️⃣ Install Needed Tools 🛠️

**Setup → Install Needed Tools** installs `squashfs-tools`, `xorriso`, `mtools`, `dosfstools` and `curl`, plus the live-boot package for your family, with your package manager (`apt`, `pacman`, `dnf`, `zypper` or `apk`):

| Family | Live-boot packages |
|--------|--------------------|
| Debian | `live-boot`, `live-boot-initramfs-tools` |
| Arch | `archiso`, `mkinitcpio-archiso`, `mkinitcpio-nfs-utils` |
| Manjaro | `manjaro-tools-iso`, `mkinitcpio-nfs-utils` |
| Fedora | `dracut-live` |

> 💡 These are installed on **your** system first, so they are part of the clone. The build itself never installs anything. Box: **Needed Tools**.
### 2️⃣ Download Bootloaders ⬇️

**Setup → Download Bootloaders** is a one-off download of the BIOS/UEFI boot files (needs internet). Box: **Bootloaders**.

### 3️⃣ Name and Folders 📂

| Setting | Description | Example |
|---------|-------------|---------|
| 📛 **Set ISO Name** | Output filename. Blank = made from distro, hostname, architecture and time | `my-backup.iso` |
| 🏗️ **Set Work Directory** | Where the build happens | `/home/claudebackup` (default) |
| 📂 **Set Output Directory** | Where the ISO is saved. Blank = the work directory | `/home/$USER/Downloads` |

### 4️⃣ Compression 🗜️

| Setting | Options |
|---------|---------|
| **Set Compression** | `zstd` (default), `xz`, `gzip` |
| **Set Compression Level** | zstd `1-22` (default `3`) |

Higher level = smaller ISO but a much slower build.

### 5️⃣ RAM Mode 🧠

**Setup → Toggle RAM Mode Boot Entry** adds a boot entry that copies the whole system into memory (`toram`).
### 6️⃣ Check the Plan 🔎

**Detected System And Build Steps** shows your distro, family, boot parameters and every step the build will run. Make sure it says **Support: yes**.

### 7️⃣ Create Bootable ISO 💿

Needs root (the app already asked), the tools and the bootloaders. The build runs:

| # | Step | What happens |
|---|------|--------------|
| 1 | **mount** | Your system is bind-mounted into a work folder (no full copy needed) |
| 2 | **bootloaders** | BIOS/UEFI boot files are copied into the ISO tree |
| 3 | **EFI image** | The FAT image UEFI boots from is built |
| 4 | **menus** | GRUB / ISOLINUX boot menus are written |
| 5 | **initramfs** | The live initramfs is built for your distro family |
| 6 | **kernel** | Kernel and initrd are copied into the ISO || 7 | **squashfs** | The system is compressed into `filesystem.squashfs` |
| 8 | **ISO** | Everything is packed with `xorriso` (BIOS + UEFI hybrid) |

🧹 Everything is unmounted at the end - also if a step fails or you press **Ctrl+C**. The finished ISO is owned by your user.

### 8️⃣ Use the ISO 🎉

- 💽 **Install ISO To USB** - pick the ISO and the drive (e.g. `/dev/sdb`). ⚠️ **Everything on that drive is erased.**
- 🧪 **Test the ISO** in a virtual machine first (enable UEFI/OVMF)
- 🖥️ **Launch Calamares** to install the system from the live session

